# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root .gitignore — repo-wide noise only.
# Per-scenario / per-service build output is handled by nested .gitignore files
# (scenario-a/, scenario-b/, frontend apps, Foundry projects, Go vendor trees).
# Keep this file focused on things that leak in at the repo root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- OS / desktop cruft ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Editor / tooling local state ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/worktrees/
.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp/
# Per-developer agent state: tool-permission allowlists and MCP server
# enablement. Committing it would publish one machine's local approvals and
# force them on everyone else. Until now this file was only kept out by whatever
# personal global ignore each developer happened to have — which protects
# nothing on a new clone or in CI, so the rule belongs here.
.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Provisioning / samples runtime data (regenerated locally) ---
# Toolkit-driven spoke/bank provisioning writes runtime state and data volumes
# next to the sample manifests; never commit these.
**/cbweb3-data/
**/.provisioning-state.yaml
**/.provisioning.lock
*.cbweb3
*.cbweb3b
scenario-a/samples/bundles
scenario-a/samples/cbweb3
scenario-b/samples/.cbweb3b
scenario-b/toolkit/samples/.cbweb3b

# --- Generated test-evidence bundles ---
# Build output, not source. Regenerate locally with the per-scenario
# `make evidence.e2e-{a,b}` targets / `tools/gen_evidence_bundles.py`.
# Includes the transient harness captures under _harness/ consumed by that generator.
/evidence-bundles/

# --- Build artifacts / transient output ---
tmp/
*.log
scenario-a/toolkit/cbweb3
